  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. The captain approved the board v2 prototype on 2026-10-07 (\"看板樣式可以了, 可以以這個版本開發\", final version v10), but the shipped board kept the old page skeleton and only took the colour tokens: the earlier v2 tasks treated the prototype as reference only and kept the existing regions. The approved prototype is kept verbatim in firstmate's local state as `state/prototypes/board-v2/` (its HTML, CSS, scripts, data snapshots and DESIGN.md with the v7 to v10 notes).",
    "What. The board's pages are ported from the prototype's HTML and CSS, which are the source of truth: the prototype's markup, styles and reading order are carried over, not described again in other words. Live data, card answering, the existing server endpoints and keyboard and screen-reader access keep working.",
    "Page skeleton. Every page has the prototype's skeleton: a sticky top bar, the full-width voyage stage, then one sticky row of four tabs (Decisions, Fleet, Crew, Log). The counts band and the separate Roster and Log summary strips are gone.",
    "Decision card. An open card reads as in the prototype: the header with the card kind, the door badge, a condensed headline and the pull request, CI and review pills; then the intent rows; then How it works and Walk the diff; the explanation, why, how and glossary sit behind \"Why you see this\", so they are no longer shown on every card by default; the decision bar is the prototype's fixed bar with signal-flag option tiles.",
    "Type, density and Fleet. Type, spacing and density follow the prototype (its font stacks, including the condensed headline face, and its type scale). On the Fleet page, task titles are clamped to three lines and the merged lane is hidden, as in the prototype.",
    "Deliberate differences. Features added after v10 stay but take the prototype's look: the animated scene and the code walk are restyled into the prototype's How it works and Walk the diff layout, and the Run retrospective control sits in the top bar in the prototype's button style. The pull request lists any other difference from the prototype, with its reason, and the designer review accepts or refuses each one.",
    "Done, pages. For each page (Decisions with an open merge card, Fleet, Crew, Log), at the designer-review viewports in light and dark, the rendered board matches the prototype's layout, reading order, type and density, apart from the deliberate differences above. Screenshots of the prototype and of the board, taken from the same data snapshot, are the evidence.",
    "Done, behaviour. The existing board behaviour still passes its end-to-end tests: answering a card, switching tabs, the theme toggle and the read-only banner. Tests that pinned the old layout (the counts band, the summary strips, the always-on explanation) are replaced by tests of the prototype layout, not kept.",
    "Out of scope. New board features, server endpoint changes beyond what the port needs, and the voyage game itself."
  ],
